-**Structural mapping:** The refraction described above is the Kha-Ba-La triad in operation. **Kha** is the witness that can notice the projection without becoming it — the capacity to see the filter and the filtered simultaneously. **Ba** is the body in Koh Phangan, the sensory apparatus that receives the bent light before the mind narrates it. **La** is the inherited pattern itself, the gravity of assumption that gives form to the formless light. Without La, there is no refraction to observe. Without Ba, there is no receiving surface. Without Kha, there is no distinction between the Moon and the story you tell about it.
+**Reading through Kha-Ba-La:** Kha names the capacity to notice a projection. Ba is the body on the island receiving light and sensation. La is the inherited expectation through which those sensations become a story. The lens gives me a way to return to the crescent without requiring the optical image to explain perception literally.